Cell[TextData[{
 "On the diamond lattice the causal order is the product order (",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 ") \[PrecedesSlantEqual] (",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["l", "TI"],
 ") \[DoubleLongLeftRightArrow] ",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 " \[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 " \[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["l", "TI"],
 ", the closed light cone of the coordinates; on a sprinkling it is the open \
light cone ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "' \[Minus] ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 " > |",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 "' \[Minus] ",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 "| of the sprinkled points. For the lattices, the sprinklings and the \
percolation an integer ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " in place of a size name gives the lattice of side ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " events; the cylinder lattice of size ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " has width and height ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 ", and a pair {",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["h", "TI"],
 "} sets them apart."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a698cee7-871b-4aa4-a384-e544590a0b88"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The option ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<KeepCoordinates\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cec5276c-7cb6-4006-906f-a473506be712"],
 " replaces the drawing layout by the construction coordinates: (",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 ") on the lattices and the 2D sprinkling. The entries ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<CubicLatticeGraph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d61bd9a6-ea1b-458b-9d8c-aa826663a318"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<MinkowskiSprinkling3D\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4274f768-7f30-410d-ad0c-b91c5c6c461d"],
 " keep their full point (",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["y", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "), and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrateHighlight"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrateHighlight", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4ae5a2d6-f5b2-47d0-90dd-bb73bb6f881d"],
 " draws them in the plane by the cabinet projection (",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["y", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 ") \[RightTeeArrow] (",
 StyleBox["x", "TI"],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["y", "TI"],
 "/(2\[Sqrt]2), ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["y", "TI"],
 "/(2\[Sqrt]2)), time up and the second space axis receding at 45\[Degree] \
with half its length, while the substrate itself keeps the 3D point. ",
 Cell[BoxData["Graph"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e5317739-43e9-4a64-9e71-bbc7962a8c45"],
 " options pass through."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"48e85bfa-5f35-43f7-ac9c-b5690c549e58"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The doc pages use ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<DiamondLatticeGraph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b1086a5-52d8-4ee6-b97b-a5c7dce59ae9"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<MinkowskiSprinkling2D\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "de249047-5b00-444f-a260-dc34bffacdf7"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<CylinderLatticeGraph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e4c082e-9d39-44c7-b8eb-1ae05c5b7f2d"],
 " at size ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Small\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c801f4aa-f892-49c5-a7b9-645435b57657"],
 " as their three substrates: a flat universe, a random one and a closed \
one."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e88884f5-c8b0-4bd9-8d79-301145595a60"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Experimental: the ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<WolframModel\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "91a4ea6b-7d1c-420e-8917-39c2a842da5a"],
 " group holds the causal graphs of six notable universes of the Wolfram \
Physics registry, \"wm3467\", \"wm7978\", \"wm4735\", \"wm1529\", \"wm3975\" \
and \"wm2216\", evolved for a fixed number of events per size and reduced to \
the Hasse diagram of their causal order. The vertices are the event numbers, \
a linear extension of the order. The edge lists ship with the paclet as the \
asset ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<WolframModelCausalGraphs\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "efc5e9a1-46ae-4ea5-9166-a5fd06d4af62"],
 ", so no evolution runs at load time. The causal orders of \"wm3467\", \
\"wm7978\" and \"wm4735\" are two-dimensional: their largest antichain and \
their longest chain both grow like the square root of the number of events \
(for \"wm7978\" at 100, 300 and 800 events the width is 12, 22 and 37 and the \
height 18, 29 and 46)."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c442975b-283e-4078-a214-f49b33cb8525"]
}, Open  ]],

